# evidence-for: FR-011, FR-039, AC-039
# evidence-volatile: \d+\.\d+s
# evidence-timeout: 300
#
# The sweep the lead asked for: every attribution, equivalence and coverage
# clause in scripts/doctype.py and tests/test_doctype.py measured against git
# history or against the code before it was left standing. Five clauses failed
# the measurement and are corrected here.
#
# 1. The comment over DOCTYPE_PY said it was read "for the two source-reading
#    tests" while the module docstring twelve lines above said three. Three is
#    right: the ast walk names them, plus the exit_one_rules helper the third
#    one calls.
#
# 2. test_architecture_is_reported_for_an_operator_and_for_a_user said its two
#    pages "differ only in their audience". They also differ in file name and in
#    title, as the two write_page calls show. The clause now claims what is
#    true -- the same two terms in the same sentence, read by different readers.
#
# 3. The comment over the `fires_on` table said "ENV_VAR, ROUTE_PATH and FLAG
#    run inside the `audience == "user"` gate". The awk slice of check_lens's
#    collection loop shows ENV_VAR's finditer at relative line 6, outside the
#    `if` at line 18: it reaches a `user` page by a condition on the match, not
#    by that gate. The behaviour the test asserts was right; the account of the
#    mechanism was not.
#
# 4. test_types_states_the_contract_the_lens_enforces said it now reads five
#    kinds against three audiences "rather than the two kinds and the one
#    audience this test first read". At 8b33f45, where the test was written, it
#    read two kinds against two audiences -- `blocks["user"]` positively and
#    `blocks["operator"]` negatively. Corrected to two.
#
# 5. doctype.py's comment over the pass line called a file it had just described
#    as changed "the byte-identical stub with the marker removed". Removing the
#    marker is a byte change. Reworded to say what was meant: nothing changed
#    but the marker taken out.
#
# Left standing after measurement, each one checked: the 20-of-27 red baseline
# and the 24-failed/10-passed worktree count (34 test functions, 27 names in the
# first index, 7 marked (control) -- 20+2+2 = 24 and 7+2+1 = 10); 2abe081's
# doctype.py blob hashing to cfafe8e's (both 0b95117); "eight" standing from
# a5484ba through seven later revisions (a5484ba..0ac652d, 1d80501 changed it);
# the census of ten at cfafe8e, 19941ad, 9859317 and 63e5e58; nine labels
# reaching defects.append with undefined-jargon the tenth through check_jargon;
# "the only exception to either" for the three source-reading tests (an ast pass
# finds no run assertion missing outcome() and no source assertion carrying it);
# the ARCH_HARD half having had no test before 0ac652d; the two pass-line guards
# having covered only the all-stub and empty trees; a5484ba's header test having
# asserted a single literal 3 against a three-term fixture; the "auditlog"
# comment as de34734 left it; survey.py's labels/commands/screens field shapes;
# four unreachable UNIVERSAL_ACRONYMS entries; five ISO_26514 rows marked
# measurable here and correctness marked measurable elsewhere.
#
# One claim could not be measured from this repository and is reported rather
# than rewritten: doctype.py:20-22 says "only 3 of Harvester's 128 pages carry a
# literal 'Overview' heading". Harvester is not in this tree, so nothing here
# can check it; inventing a replacement number would be the failure class this
# sweep exists to close.
#
